  "research": {
    "summary": "Current work designs and applies data- and physics-based models for engineering, science, and biomedicine, with emphasis on scientific machine learning, inverse problems, conditional generative models, diffusion and flow-matching methods, data assimilation, reduced-order modeling, and multiscale mechanics. Recent applications include renal tumor classification, medical-image harmonization, rare-event cell phenotyping, fluorescence imaging, and probabilistic wildfire reconstruction and forecasting.",
